Say what a custom view placeholder became, and what the nib sized a view to.

Two traces for one question: the iTerm2 Preferences pane is zero by zero, so the window that now
opens is only as tall as its own chrome. A view that is zero and is never sent setFrame: afterwards
has only its decode, and nothing printed what that decode produced.

CIDER_TRACE_CUSTOMVIEW prints, for every NSCustomView placeholder, the NSClassName it carried, the
class it actually became, the frame, and whether the archive held NSFrame or NSFrameSize.
CIDER_TRACE_SVFRAME, which already selected a class for the setFrame traces, now also prints the
frame decoded by -[NSView initWithCoder:] for that class, which is the only other place a nib
decoded view can get a size.

WHAT THEY MEASURED, so the next attempt starts from evidence and not from this list again. Every
one of these is a refuted explanation for the zero sized pane:

  104 placeholders decode in the Preferences nib and every one becomes a real class at a real size
      (NSView, ProfileListView, sizes from 525x279 to 922x420). Not one is zero.
  NSCustomView is sent setFrame: or setFrameSize: ZERO times in a whole run. The control is the
      same trace widened to any class name containing View, which prints 1360 frame events across
      NSClipView, NSTableHeaderView, NSImageView, NSView and nine others in the same run, so the
      silence is real and not a dead instrument.
  No class in that nib fails to resolve. CIDER_NIB archive NO CLASS never fires and the NSCustomView
      unknown class log never fires, with 479 other NSLog lines in the same capture proving the
      channel works.
  Nothing in this tree sets translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints to NO. Both assignments in
      NSView.m set it to YES, and -[NSView init] gives 1x1 rather than zero, so the application
      turned it off itself.

So the pane is an NSCustomView instance carrying the zero initialised ivars of a bare alloc: frame
zero, autoresizing mask zero, translates NO, no subviews. Every path in this framework that builds
one from an archive sets at least one of those, and none of them ran for it. Where it comes from is
the open question, and the traces above are what will answer it.

